  ("h2", "Request Lifecycle"),
  ("p", "Every conversation, inbound or outbound, follows one lifecycle: channel ingress (phone call, chat message, SMS, webhook), gateway (media gateway for audio, API gateway for events), the AI orchestrator, which resolves employee configuration, permissions, and context policy; context and memory assembly from organization-scoped stores; worker routing to the specialist workers; external provider calls where required; response streaming back to the channel; and usage events written for metering, audit, and analytics. The orchestrator is deliberately thin: it decides who works, with what permissions, on what data, and when to escalate. It does not itself transform audio or generate text, which keeps the brain auditable and the workers replaceable."),
