  ("h2", "Turn-Taking and Interruption"),
  ("p", "Interruption handling is a safety-gated behavior, not a random feature. While the AI speaks, VAD continues listening; caller speech crossing a threshold immediately fades AI audio out within 150 ms, aborts pending TTS, and marks the generation as interrupted so the LLM receives the new utterance with conversational context. The AI may itself interrupt the customer only under gated conditions: urgent correction (the customer states something factually wrong that the business rules flag), clarification that prevents a misunderstanding, or acknowledgement-style backchannels that humans naturally use. Every AI-initiated interruption is logged with its gate classification, because an AI that constantly interrupts is a defect, and the log is how the behavior gets tuned."),
  ("h2", "Naturalness Standards"),
  ("p", "The voice must not sound like an assistant reading a script. Standards applied in tuning and QA: prosody varies with sentence type; pauses follow punctuation and thought boundaries; short acknowledgements are used the way humans use them; speaking speed adapts to the caller's measured rate; hesitation appears only where a human would hesitate, for example before delivering a number that was just looked up. Forbidden by policy: unnecessary beeps, fake hold music, please wait filler while nothing is being checked, confirmation of every sentence, monotone delivery, and dead air while a tool executes. When a tool runs, the employee says something true about it, then reports the real result."),
