  ("p", "Voice cloning is optional, permission-gated, and revocable by design. The consent record stores the voice owner, authorization status, consent timestamp, allowed usage scope, voice ID, creation date, revocation state, and full audit history. Cloning cannot be initiated without an explicit consent artifact (recorded attestation or signed document); usage scope limits where the cloned voice may be deployed; and revocation is immediate, removing the voice from all employees and blocking any in-flight synthesis. The schema in Chapter 7 treats consent as data lineage: a voice without a valid consent record is not loadable by the TTS worker, enforced at the query layer rather than by UI convention."),
